{"name":"Monsoon","hex":"#7a7679","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"monsoon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a number of winds associated with regions where most rain falls during a particular season.","Tropical rainy season when the rain lasts for several months with few interruptions."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monsoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monsoon","blocks":[{"text":"A monsoon is traditionally a seasonal reversing wind accompanied by corresponding changes in precipitation, but now used to describe seasonal changes in atmospheric circulation and precipitation associated with annual latitudinal oscillation of the Intertropical Convergence Zone, specifically between its limits to the north and south of the equator."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Monsoon_clouds_near_Nagercoil.jpg/330px-Monsoon_clouds_near_Nagercoil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monsoon","wikidata":"Q42967"},{"title":"Monsoon (2019 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Monsoon is a 2019 British drama film, written and directed by Hong Khaou and produced by Tracy O'Riordan. It stars Henry Golding, Parker Sawyers, David Tran and Molly Harris."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8c/Monsoon_poster.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monsoon_(2019_film)","wikidata":"Q64900128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Monsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg/500px-Monsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Monsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg/500px-Monsoon_clouds_arriving_at_Port_Blair%2C_Andaman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedi